# PnS flow-delivery subagent routing

When `.local-orchestrator/flow-delivery-lease.json` exists with
`workflow: pns-flow-delivery`, the parent may invoke only:

- `pns-flow-recon`
- `pns-flow-implementer`
- `pns-flow-reviewer`
- `pns-evidence-reviewer`

Do not invoke built-in, automatically selected, or other custom subagents during that delivery
lease. Only `pns-flow-implementer` may write, and only one invocation of it may be active. A named
subagent must never spawn another subagent. The parent alone selects tasks, accepts architecture,
issues correction instructions, runs the full suite, owns BlueStacks input, accepts evidence,
commits, and changes queue state.

Launch every named agent only through one foreground Cursor IDE native `Subagent`/`Task` tool call
visible in the current parent conversation. Explicitly set the named `pns-*` agent and model
`cursor-grok-4.5-high`. Wait for its terminal result before continuing. Cursor CLI, `cursor-agent`,
`agent`, terminal subprocesses, SDK, ACP, MCP, slash-command prose, `/multitask`, detached parents,
and direct-parent substitution are forbidden. If native delegation is unavailable, stop with
`IDE_NATIVE_SUBAGENT_TOOL_UNAVAILABLE`; never fall back.

Authorization boundary: project `preToolUse(Task)` is the fail-closed gate before child creation.
`subagentStart` is audit-only for resolved-identity receipts and must not be treated as the
mechanism that prevents child creation. Denied Task requests must not silently fall back.

Outside an active PnS flow-delivery lease, this rule does not restrict ordinary Cursor usage.
